# 2026-08-11 front-end rebuild.  The pattern list above is per-extension, which
# is not enough here: the ingest writes whole clip *directories* (mp4 + wav +
# npy + npz + json), and json is not ignored, so a blanket `git add` would
# commit tens of thousands of meta.json files pointing at data that is not in
# git.  Ignore the trees, the way /third_party/TMR/ is ignored.
/data/wild_ingest_v1
/data/wild_videos_20260811
/data/wild_videos_converted*/
/data/wild_videos_pending_3d/
/data/wild_videos_redo_3d/
/data/wild_visual_s3d_*/
/data/wild3d/ingest_v1_*/
/data/atomic_aistpp
/runs
# DWPose's ONNX weights are 335 MB and live in the OSS store like the rest of
# third_party; the vendored source next to them is small and *is* tracked.
/third_party/DWPose/weights/
/third_party/PoseScript/

# 2026-08-12: the workspace NAS quota filled, so these moved into the asset
# cache and are symlinks now.  A trailing slash would not match a symlink --
# the same trap /third_party/GVHMR hit.
/data/wild_videos_20260811

# NFS silly-rename leftovers.  Replacing a script that running shells hold
# open leaves one of these until the last reader exits -- which is the sign
# the atomic swap worked, not a problem.
.nfs*

# 2026-08-17: /data/aistpp_official and /data/wild_ingest_v1 were written with a
# trailing slash on the line right below the note saying a trailing slash does
# not match a symlink, and both had since become symlinks into the asset cache.
# Third and fourth time.  The rule is: never a trailing slash on anything under
# /data or /third_party, because anything there may be evicted to /cache and come
# back as a link (tools/oss_assets.py pull --cache does exactly that).
# Reference PDFs, alongside the existing block above.
/PoseScript.pdf
/WGHMR.pdf
/zero-shot natural language video localization.pdf
# ossutil writes a .report per transfer next to the CWD.
/ossutil_output
# Rendered example pages; the tool that makes them is the artifact.
/output
.venv_*

# SMPL body models: licence-gated downloads, 800 MB, and reproducible from the
# vendor's own zip by the one-time chumpy conversion recorded in worklog:3931.
# The UV unwrap, the appearance texture and the body-part segmentation DO belong
# here -- they are small, they are what a render's look depends on, and their
# provenance is in third_party/smpl_models/uv/PROVENANCE.md.
/third_party/smpl_models/*.pkl
/third_party/smpl_models/*.zip
# The VRM avatar is a 10 MB vendor sample; PROVENANCE.md records where to get it.
/third_party/vrm/*.glb

# Per-machine Claude Code settings; the .local suffix means not shared.
.claude/settings.local.json

